dot(R,blue);
label("$\mathbf{x}_{3}$",R,blue);
[/asy]

Then the matrix of projections onto the plane $P$ is simply the product of the matrices $AE.$  Alternatively, we can let $\mathbf{n}$ be the normal vector of $P$ and let $\mathbf{p}$ be any point in the plane $P.$  We then have that the matrix of projections onto $P$ is $(\mathbf{n} \cdot  \mathbf{p})E.$  Solving, we find the normal vector to be
